//P3 review Important-2 (explicit form): a bare `this` in a ctor default is
//rejected. Defaults evaluate at the call site, where the object under
//construction does not exist yet — the reference used to fall back to the
//caller's local 0 and silently read the caller's object (or crash with a
//null reference from main). 0.13.13a D-5: the wording says 'this' because
//this spelling holds an explicit this and no member binding to name.
class Vec {
    public int a;
    public int b;
    public Vec(int x, int y = this) {
        this.a = x; this.b = y;    }
}

int main() {
    Vec v = Vec(7);
    return 0;
}
